    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Brendan Donovan** (68.26) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.48) anchor our production floor, both boasting elite efficiency scores. **Brendan Donovan** is the primary beneficiary of a favorable matchup against Hayden Wesneski; his strong platoon advantage against the right-hander provides a significant 14% boost to his output. Similarly, **Gleyber Torres** (67.46) is a high-upside play, leveraging a strong platoon edge against a lefty and the optimal leadoff spot to maximize run-scoring potential. **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.23) also warrants attention; while his park factor is slightly suppressive, his matchup against Michael Lorenzen combined with his propensity to exploit slow deliveries for stolen base opportunities makes him a high-efficiency asset in our pursuit of category scarcity.\n\nThe lineup construction prioritizes power and platoon mitigation, though we must navigate the uncertainty of several \"Lineup Pending\" designations. **Zack Gelof** (58.71) is a critical start tonight, as the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a substantial platoon advantage against MacKenzie Gore overrides a mediocre opposing xERA. Conversely, we have opted to bench **JJ Bleday** (48.77), who finished as the top external candidate. While **JJ Bleday** showed promise in our modeling, his scoring profile was hampered by a negative platoon shift against Ryan Gusto and, more importantly, a 40% rain risk warning that introduced unnecessary variance compared to the reliability of **Daulton Varsho** (53.86) or **Lawrence Butler** (50.29). \n\nWe are monitoring the **Cal Raleigh** (61.74) and **Yainer Diaz** (45.40) situations closely; **Cal Raleigh** remains a high-floor play due to the weakness of the opposing starter, but **Yainer Diaz** is currently operating at the bottom of our threshold, heavily penalized by an assumed spot in the bottom third of the order. While we have bench depth in **Justin Crawford** and **Gavin Sheets**, their current metrics suggest they are secondary options. We will proceed with the current configuration, banking on the platoon edges of **Jonathan Aranda** (60.85) and **Bryce Harper** (61.17) to provide the necessary stability to maintain our 5x5 pace.",
